  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "Can AI actually make you money?",
      "answer": "Yes, but primarily by doing paid hourly or project work using AI tools. High-demand routes include data annotation contracts, technical freelancing, and building software automations. Unsupervised passive income systems rarely generate stable returns."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which AI tool is best for earning money?",
      "answer": "The right tool depends entirely on your target service. ChatGPT Plus and Claude Pro assign commercial rights for generated text, code, and project analysis. For automation agencies, platforms like n8n, Make, and Zapier handle business workflows."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I make $1,000 a day using AI?",
      "answer": "There is no credible evidence supporting turnkey systems that yield $1,000 per day. The FTC has shut down operations like Ascend Ecom and Click Profit for making unsubstantiated automated earnings claims that resulted in millions of dollars in consumer losses."
    },
    {
      "question": "How can I train AI and earn money?",
      "answer": "You can apply as an independent contractor on data annotation platforms like DataAnnotation, Mindrift, Alignerr, or Handshake AI. Contractors take screening tests to evaluate model responses, audit factual claims, and review code."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I make money with AI with no experience?",
      "answer": "Entry-level microtask platforms like Prolific pay participants a minimum of $8 per hour for surveys and evaluations. While Mindrift lists entry-level projects at $15 to $30 per hour, platforms like DataAnnotation generally seek candidates with bachelor's degrees or equivalent professional backgrounds."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is AI passive income real?",
      "answer": "True passive income with AI is largely a myth. Generating ad revenue on YouTube, selling digital assets, or licensing music requires ongoing human creative direction, manual editing, compliance tracking, and platform maintenance."
    }
  ],
